across the Marvel Cinematic Universe as  many movies countless epic fights have  unfolded we've seen incredible showdowns  between the likes of Thor and Hulk Hulk  in the Hulkbuster Captain America and  Red Skull and so many more  however for as many cool fight scenes as  there are across the MCU filmography  it's pretty obvious that some conflicts  in the MCU are inherently more  captivating than their peers these are  the greatest fight scenes in the MCU  Captain America vs Iron Man this fight  in Captain America Civil War is the  payoff to over half a decade's worth of  tension building between the MC use two  biggest heroes across both Avengers  movies we'd see these fan favorite  characters butt heads while their solo  movies push them even farther into  different perspectives that kind of  friction could only be resolved in one  way and audiences were waiting for it  the scene led us revel in seen our  favorite hero beat the snot out of the  other guy and gave us an MCU fight with  some actual emotional stakes another  excellent aspect of the fight is how  close it is to its comic book  counterpart in terms of general tone and  shot composure  the battle pays tribute to its source  material without being limited by it and  raises the MCU cinematography standards  all inside a few short sweet minutes the  Hydra fortress assault courtesy of  Avengers age of Ultron this fight scene  from the moment it begins is an absolute  joy not only does it display each of the  core Avengers and all their glory but it  does so through the use of one  continuous shot that strings together  the different Avengers in a sweeping  interconnected style every avenger gets  their time to shine as icing on the cake  the opening scene caps off with a  beautiful group shot of all the Avengers  leaping into battle as a combined unit  and it's at that moment you're reminded  why Marvel's interconnected universe was  worth all the effort  [Music]  iron man's assault on terrorism it's one  